 ahead and browse  this which is pretty cool so for example  i could maybe want to view something  like top down here  i don't know for whatever reason so  let's just leave this here  maybe this i'll pop over here let's go  ahead and like drag in a new object like  a sphere  maybe like into here and we'll move it  upwards  and you can see that i can kind of like  play around with this i mean i can  position it here  i can position it here the gizmo is  basically whatever viewport you've got  highlighted if you've got like a gizmo  selected  like you know translate rotate scale  whatever if your mouse is over  like a certain viewport the gizmo will  only kind of display i guess in render  on that particular viewport so i can  like move this around  drag in like a little cone or whatever  might be easier to move it from here  that's the entire sponsor i knew that  would happen let's go back to the cone  and you can see that we have this like  cone here that we can edit and  like i mean i think you kind of get the  point so having multiple viewports is  kind of cool again not like strictly a  requirement that  we needed but i guess this is kind of  cool for the future especially if we  kind of have like  four of these i guess have them have  some of them in wireframe have like left  top what else is there back  front whatever have those kind of um  like 3dmax style  i guess that's where i remember it from  um but basically have like a bunch of  you boss maybe some of them not fully  shaded because obviously this does still  cost something  surprisingly the rendering cost for  having two viewports is actually not  that  not that much greater i mean the  rendering cost itself is  is really not that much greater because  if you haven't noticed now there's  suddenly half the pixels  so we've made the viewport smaller it  still has to like render all the all of  the geometry from a different point of  view  obviously but it does work pretty well  um and i think that it's pretty cool to  be able to do  stuff like this and then kind of see the  effects i guess on multiple viewports so  yeah that's a pretty cool side effect  and of course this viewport itself you  can just kind of  drag it out and you can put it on a  second monitor which you guys can't  really see but i could put this  anywhere i guess and uh where did i just  put it here  um let's make this a little bit bigger  you can put this wherever you like um  and of course it will like work properly  and everything  will be great let's just put it back  here because i think it belongs here  all right that's better so anyway i hope  you guys enjoyed this little look at  what i have done in the last week  um for the next week ahead i have  actually like the next few day vlogs the  next few weeks  are going to be really cool like i  promise you guys like i don't want to  reveal anything just  yet but we are working on some really  cool things and perhaps the most  exciting thing of all  is that like in the works right now like  i have a game  that i'm working on that i will that  should not take  more than like a few weeks of actual  development time  this is not like a large scale project  that i'm going to work on for the next  few years  but i actually have a game idea that i  want to make inside hazel  like within like the next couple months  for sure  so all of these features that are going  in now and some other ones that i'll  talk about next week  um they're all kind of building up  towards an actual real project so i'm  super excited about that as i mentioned  in the beginning this wouldn't be  possible without all the lovely patrons  helping to support the development of  hazel  so if you would like to help support the  development of hazel and get access to  like the source code and hazel itself  and all of that stuff then go to  patreon.com  there'll be a link in description below  and thank you so much for your support  now i mentioned a lot about like  re-architecting